      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Challenge: Incorrect longitude signs can misplace a hurricane track\n",
        "\n",
        "The original Hurricane Florence CSV stores longitude as a positive degrees-west magnitude. However, in the standard WGS 84 coordinate system, locations west of the Prime Meridian have negative longitude values. If these positive values are used directly to create geographic points, the hurricane will appear in the wrong part of the world. This is a data interpretation challenge rather than a typographical error. To solve it, the longitude values must be converted to negative values before creating the GeoDataFrame."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "s_Z0fTtbkkHU"
      },
      "id": "s_Z0fTtbkkHU"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Load the original CSV data without correcting longitude\n",
        "florence_original = pd.read_csv(track_path)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Inspect the original longitude and latitude values\n",
        "print(florence_original[[\"Long\", \"Lat\"]].head())\n",
        "\n",
        "# Create a GeoDataFrame with the incorrect longitude signs\n",
        "gdf_wrong = gpd.GeoDataFrame(\n",
        "    florence_original,\n",
        "    geometry=gpd.points_from_xy(\n",
        "        florence_original[\"Long\"],\n",
        "        florence_original[\"Lat\"]\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "    crs=\"EPSG:4326\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Plot the incorrectly located hurricane track\n",
        "gdf_wrong.plot(figsize=(10, 6), color=\"red\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Hurricane Florence: Incorrect Longitude Signs\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
